# Tests

`npm test` builds the bundle and drives three pages through headless Chrome. Needs Chrome or
Edge installed; `CHROME=<path>` overrides detection.

| Page | Covers |
|------|--------|
| `src/selftest.js` | Maths against the real bundle — the GPU warp versus the CPU implementation, homography, lens |
| `src/inttest.js` | End to end through store, canvases, warp, material and export, driven as the UI drives them |
| `src/uitest.js` | The mounted app under synthetic pointer events — docking, panels, selection |

Every behaviour change lands with a check at the matching level, in the same commit. A feature
with no check is unfinished.

Run `npm test` before pushing, not just before a release: `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs the same
suite on every push and pull request, and again on a `v*` tag - where a failure stops the release
and the deployment, so red at a tag means the published page does not update.

- Add checks with the page's own `check(name, ok, detail)` — the runner looks for
  `RESULT: ALL PASSED` and nothing else counts as a pass.
- Never delete, skip or loosen a check to make the suite green. Fix the cause.
- Never call work done on a red suite, and never leave `main` red.
- A release also needs the suite run against the built artefact, which `npm test` already does —
  it tests `dist/test/*.html`, not the sources.
